{"pageProps":{"fileName":"2026-06-02-location-spot-queenvictoriabuilding","title":"Queen Victoria Building","cover":"/assets/snippets/location/246db0d53aca5500238ef4bad2fcc232.jpg","tags":["spot"],"date":"2026-06-02","review":"A spot everyone seems to visit when they come to Sydney. Built in 1898, the Romanesque architecture and stained glass make it a building that truly captures the grandeur of Western design. There was a free photo booth event running inside the building.","description":"","series":"location","type":"snippets","postKey":"fc433c88ab939696a0900e256835f94b","content":"\n<center>\n<RestaurantCard\n  cover=\"/assets/snippets/location/246db0d53aca5500238ef4bad2fcc232.jpg\"\n  title=\"Queen Victoria Building\"\n  cuisine=\"Spot\"\n  address=\"455 George St, Sydney NSW 2000 Australia\"\n  rating=3.5\n  tags=\"spot\"\n/>\n</center>\n\n## Review\nA spot everyone seems to visit when they come to Sydney.  \nBuilt in `1898`, the Romanesque architecture and stained glass make it a building that truly captures the grandeur of Western design.\n\nThere was a free <mark>photo booth</mark> event running inside the building.  \nWe waited a bit, but it was fun and the print quality came out better than expected — very satisfying.\n```adcard\n```\nThere are also several restaurants and cafes inside, so dining there would be a great option if you get the chance.\n\nInside the building, you'll find the `Royal Clock` that moves on the hour and the `Great Australian Clock` depicting Australian history.  \nAdmission is free, and guided tours run on Tuesdays, Thursdays, and Sundays at 11:30 AM.  \nThe building narrowly escaped demolition in `1959` and was fully restored by `1986` to become what it is today.  \n## Pictures\n<pictures>\n<img src=\"/assets/snippets/location/246db0d53aca5500238ef4bad2fcc232.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; object-fit: contain;\" alt=\"Queen Victoria Building\">\n<img src=\"/assets/snippets/location/80b474f7d66a9be908cb4d3929ac384d.j